  "query_preview": "..High pressure will remain the main feature of \nthe forecast as it weakens and pushes to the north over the \nweekend. By early next week, the high will slide over the Four \nCorners region. \n\nFor today, expect similar conditions to the past few days with \nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms. Storms will \ninitiate across the higher terrain by early afternoon, moving off \ntowards the south and west through this evening. Instability \nremains marginal so can't rule out a few strong to severe \nstorms, mainly over Yavapai and Gila counties. Heavy rain with the \npotential for flash flooding will remain the main hazard. \n\nToday should be the end of the very hot temperatures we have \nseen up in the Grand Canyon and Glen/Marble Canyons for the past \nweek or so. With increasing moisture, storm coverage, and cloud \ncover, the heat will finally break, allowing for the Extreme Heat \nWarning to finally expire this evening. \n\nThe active monsoon pattern will hold through next week as the high \nremains near or over the Four Corners region. Temperatures will \ncool across the region and will see scattered to numerous showers \nand thunderstorms each day. Overall, expect the monsoon to become \nthe main story for the next week.",
